/// `messages.sendStory` params (contract revision 1.76, §4.67; the
/// link-preview metadata keys joined with 1.91, §4.74): the story text plus
/// the caller-computed recipient expansion. There is no `clientRequestId`
/// and no conversation addressing: a story lands in no conversation row, so
/// there is no pending row to dedupe or settle (the result is synchronous;
/// the sender's own timeline converges through the desktop's own
/// bookkeeping of the returned timestamp, the official sendStory job
/// shape). `distributionListId` is optional — absent means the official
/// MY_STORY id; any other valid UUID passes through as a desktop-owned
/// custom list (the desktop holds v1 list storage, members ride
/// `recipients` explicitly). `previewUrl`/`previewTitle` are independently
/// optional link-preview metadata: each validates fail-closed (the §4.74
/// ladder) and rides the engine frame verbatim; absent means the key is
/// never sent.
///
/// Contract 1.156 (§4.154): the story body itself is optional — `message`
/// is the text story leg and `attachment` (the engine's media story batch,
/// engine `7e3652e`, the official `StoryMessage.fileAttachment` alignment)
/// is the media story leg. The connector performs no leg-exclusivity gate:
/// message/attachment co-presence, a text-leg key riding the attachment
/// leg, and a bare no-payload frame are all the engine's fail-closed parse
/// (its plain -32603 through the structured ladder) — the connector only
/// forwards what arrived. The attachment data URI is verbatim transit
/// material: no deep parse, no cap check (the upload/cap gates are the
/// engine's transit-CDN face).
///
/// Contract 1.157 (§4.155): `group` is the group audience leg (the
/// engine's group story batch, engine `ffab2a8`, the official
/// `StoryMessage.group` GroupContextV2 alignment) — the recipients empty
/// batch, locally refused since 1.76, now forwards when the group leg
/// rides (the group single leg; the engine's own audience-at-least-one-domain
/// gate mirrored) and keeps its refusal when the group leg is absent. The
/// mixed audience (group + recipients) forwards as-is — the multi-domain
/// orchestration is the engine's, never a connector gate. The additive
/// response face `group: {groupId, timestamp}` passes through the
/// projection untouched (absent stays absent, never null — every
/// pre-1.157 response reads byte-identically).
#[derive(Debug, Deserialize)]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase", deny_unknown_fields)]
pub struct MessagesSendStoryParams {
    pub account_id: String,
    pub message: Option<String>,
    pub recipients: Vec<String>,
    pub distribution_list_id: Option<String>,
    #[serde(default)]
    pub allows_replies: bool,
    pub text_style: Option<String>,
    pub body_ranges: Option<Vec<SendTextStyleParams>>,
    pub preview_image: Option<String>,
    pub preview_url: Option<String>,
    pub preview_title: Option<String>,
    /// The media story leg: one attachment data URI (the upstream
    /// `data:<mediatype>[;filename=<pct>][;voice=true][;gif=true];base64,`
    /// shape) forwarded verbatim — the connector never parses the content
    /// and never gates the value domain (empty string included; the
    /// engine's parse owns the refusal).
    pub attachment: Option<String>,
    /// Contract 1.185 (§4.185): the media story's caption — the engine
    /// caption face (engine `48e69a2`, the official `AttachmentPointer.caption`
    /// alignment, the caption riding the upload's returned pointer) riding
    /// the engine `sendStory` frame verbatim on the attachment leg's class
    /// (the 1.156 attachment posture): the connector performs no leg gate and
    /// no byte gate — the caption is verbatim transit material, the engine's
    /// documented parse owning the whole value domain (a non-string or empty
    /// caption, a caption over the official MAX_BODY_ATTACHMENT_BYTE_LENGTH
    /// 64 KiB budget, and a caption riding without the attachment leg are all
    /// its plain -32603, degrading through the structured ladder to
    /// UPSTREAM_ERROR retryable). A JSON null folds to None at the serde
    /// option layer (the §4.154 with_nulls precedent): neither absent nor
    /// null ever reaches the frame.
    pub caption: Option<String>,
    /// Contract 1.157 (§4.155): the group audience leg — the engine groupId
    /// (the group master key standard base64, the `sendTextGroup` group-id
    /// caliber) riding the engine `sendStory` frame verbatim. The key stays
    /// a raw JSON value on purpose (the 1.153 three-key and 1.156 timestamp
    /// posture): the engine's documented gate owns the whole value domain —
    /// a non-string or empty group answers its plain -32603, a non-32B
    /// group id its decode refusal, a terminated group and an
    /// announcements-only non-admin group its structured -1
    /// `SEND_TARGET_*` faces — and connector-side typing would eat the
    /// non-string face, answering a local INVALID_REQUEST (different code,
    /// different retryability) instead of forwarding the engine's
    /// UPSTREAM_ERROR ladder. A JSON null folds to None at the serde option
    /// layer (the §4.154 with_nulls precedent): neither absent nor null
    /// ever reaches the gates or the frame.
    pub group: Option<Value>,
}

